Notebook-AI @VERSION@  -  Windows (@ARCH@) distribution
=======================================================

Offline handwritten-text OCR for the desktop: open photos or scans, prepare them (rotate / straighten / crop),
extract the text, review and correct it, keep many pages in one project file, export UTF-8 text.
Nothing leaves your machine: there is no network access at run time.

*** STATUS: this Windows distribution has been assembled and statically verified, but it has NOT yet been
*** executed on a real Windows machine by its maintainers. Treat it as a test build until that is done.

WHAT THIS PACKAGE CONTAINS
  app\            the application (JavaFX 21 and ONNX Runtime for Windows x64 only) and the OCR models
                  (PP-OCRv6_small detector + recognizer, Apache-2.0) - everything needed to run OCR offline
  install.cmd     per-user installer           uninstall.cmd   removes what install.cmd installed
  run-notebook-ai.cmd   run in place, without installing
  scripts\ licenses\ LICENSE THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt   helpers + legal documents
  distribution.json  SHA256SUMS             metadata and checksums of every shipped file

WHAT YOU MUST INSTALL YOURSELF (not included)
  * Java 21 or newer (a JRE is enough), on PATH or via JAVA_HOME. No Java runtime is bundled. Check:  java -version
  * Windows PowerShell 5.1 or newer (part of Windows 10/11) - used by the installer only.
  Supported: Windows x64 only. ARM64 and 32-bit Windows are not supported.

STEP 1 - EXTRACT
  Extract the whole ZIP (right-click > Extract All...). Do not run files from inside the ZIP viewer.
  Spaces in the path are fine. Optional integrity check of the archive:
      certutil -hashfile notebook-ai-@VERSION@-windows-@ARCH@.zip SHA256   (compare with the .sha256 file)

STEP 2a - JUST RUN IT (no installation)
  run-notebook-ai.cmd
  Works from any directory, checks your Java version, writes nothing into this folder.
  Self-test without a window:   run-notebook-ai.cmd --self-check

STEP 2b - INSTALL FOR YOUR USER (no Administrator rights)
  install.cmd --add-to-path
  Installs to   %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\Notebook-AI   with the command   %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\Notebook-AI\bin\notebook-ai.cmd
  --add-to-path is your explicit consent to add that bin folder to YOUR user PATH (existing entries are kept).
  Without it nothing on PATH changes and the exact command path is printed. Open a NEW Command Prompt afterwards,
  then type:   notebook-ai
  The installed command keeps working if you move or delete this extracted folder. Options: install.cmd --help
  The installer refuses to run from an elevated (Administrator) prompt. It does not change any PowerShell
  execution policy (it uses a process-scoped bypass for its own script only).

UPGRADE
  Extract the new ZIP and run its install.cmd again. The old installation is replaced as a whole and restored if
  anything fails. If Notebook-AI is running, close it first (Windows locks its files). Your projects (.nbai) are never touched.

UNINSTALL
  uninstall.cmd             (same --app-dir option as you installed with)
  Removes only the installation owned by the installer, and a PATH entry only if install.cmd added it.
  Your projects, exports and other programs stay.

IF SOMETHING GOES WRONG
  "Java 21 or newer is required"  -> install Java 21+ or set JAVA_HOME.
  "failed its SHA256SUMS integrity check" -> extract the ZIP again.
  'notebook-ai' is not recognized -> PATH was not changed or the window is old: open a NEW Command Prompt,
      or run install.cmd --add-to-path, or use the full path printed by the installer.

LICENSES
  Notebook-AI is BSD 3-Clause (LICENSE). Third-party components and their licenses are listed in
  THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt; the texts are in licenses\. Please read the "known gaps" section there.

